  "notes": "Compound of {分|ぶん} (to divide) + {割|かつ} (to split). A common word in finance, technology, and everyday contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {分割|ぶんかつ}する (to divide, to split)\n- {分割|ぶんかつ}{払|ばら}い (installment payment)\n- {分割|ぶんかつ}{統治|とうち} (divide and rule)\n- {画面|がめん}{分割|ぶんかつ} (split screen)\n- {株式|かぶしき}{分割|ぶんかつ} (stock split)\n- {分割|ぶんかつ}ファイル (split file)\n- 〜を{二|ふた}つに{分割|ぶんかつ}する (to divide ~ into two)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {分割|ぶんかつ}: dividing one thing into defined parts (often deliberate, planned)\n- {分離|ぶんり}: separating things that were connected\n- {分裂|ぶんれつ}: splitting apart, often with a sense of conflict or fragmentation",
